A||||12||V8Dreamer||Headliner Fabric....Where to find?||||7||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||09-10-2001||05:51 PM||||Well, the headliner is sadly sagging in my GT and I think it's time to replace it.  I was wondering if anyone could tell me where I could get (preferably order) gray headliner fabric to re-upholster the headliner.  Reusing the old fabric is out of the question since the previous owner used the "staple method" to hold it up when it began to come undone.<P>TIA,<BR>Ryan<P>btw, I also need to get some black headliner fabric for my black interior in my coupe...so this info will be even more helpful now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000001||skitime||09-10-2001||05:57 PM||||Wow, another Fiero in our area.  I don't remember you before so let me say hi. The headlining material is often available at places like Autozone.  I got ours from a auto reupholstery shop.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||09-10-2001||05:58 PM||||You can't reuse the old stuff anyway.  The reason it sags is that the foam backing has detiorated and come of the back of the fabric.  <P>You can pick up headliner at a local auto upholstery shop.  They will have any color you want and it is cheap.  I spent about $14 on the headliner material and a can of the spray adhesive they recommended.  Had enuff left over for my wife to make new sun visor covers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||snafus87||09-10-2001||05:58 PM||||I'm not sure where Fleabitdog got the material...but the stuff he used for mine is much nicer than the original stuff that was there...<P>Maybe he'll reply and let you know...<P>If you are interested I live in Lehighton and perhaps I could show you the job he did on mine...just a thought...since someone else has a Fiero relatively close to me...<P>Good luck...sorry I couldn't really tell you where to get stuff...don't really know what's around here...only living in the area for about 5 months...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||09-10-2001||06:19 PM||||Skitime, you already know V8Dreamer, you just haven't made the connection yet. Ryan is one of the guys that was with me at the Zinn's show and the Carlisle show, he drives the yellow 2M4 with the extractor hood. Remember him? Well, you're better off not knowing him anyway, I wish I didn't!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I already told him where to get the fabric, but I guess he's too lazy to drive two miles from his house to get it. What a geek!||||reg||7
Z||000005||Oreif||09-10-2001||06:22 PM||||You can pick up a headliner kit called "Heads Up". It's available in many colors.<BR>For sale at Trak Auto, AutoZone, PepBoys, ETC. The Heads Up stuff is thicker than what you'd get at a fabric shop. I don't know about stuff from an upholstery shop.||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||09-10-2001||07:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>Skitime, you already know V8Dreamer, you just haven't made the connection yet. Ryan is one of the guys that was with me at the Zinn's show and the Carlisle show, he drives the yellow 2M4 with the extractor hood. Remember him? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yes, I remember him but you are right I didn't make the connection or realize he had a V8 Fiero.  Or is the V8Dreamer still a dream.  BTW, Rockcrawl I still love your hood vents you made for his car.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fleabitdog||09-10-2001||10:52 PM||||I got the first headliner material from the uph- shop ski uses in Akron. The second I got at an uph-shop in Pottstown. They were both the same material just different shades by my choosing. It is excellent material. I even did my backerboard with it. Go with the spray adhesive though. It is much easier than brushing contact cement. Rockcrawl any luck at that yard? Snafus, are you still looking for a third brakelite w/ wiring? Give me a yell. Ski, tell Denny if he quit parking in the woods by the cricks he wouldn't find that fishing line on his car. Also V8 Dreamer, if you should find yourself needing another headliner board I have them. For an additional price it can come with new material on it and for another additional price it will be installed. Dave  <p>[This message has been edited by Fleabitdog (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||My7Fieros||09-11-2001||12:33 AM||||I got mine at a fabric store (Hancock Fabrics)...it was in a bin labled (fittingly enough) "automotive headliner". I about sh!t myself when I saw it. They even had the oem colors tan and grey! Best part was it was only a few bucks a yard. Its a foamy kinda fabric, not thin like other fabrics. Take down the headliner board, pull off your old fabric, clean the board, and apply that 3M spray glue generously to the board and fabric and apply. Cut around sunroof hole if applicable, and reinstall the rubber "ring' thing around the sunroof hole. Easy job and very cheap as well. Ive done it to all my Fieros.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Loki||09-11-2001||12:39 AM||||The stuff form Pep-Boys works GREAT!!!!!  Did the headliner in my 86SE black and it turned out AWSOME!! Even impressed my dad   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000010||V8Dreamer||09-11-2001||12:59 AM||||Ski -- the V8 Fiero is definately still a dream.....far off in the distance.  Thanks everyone for the responses....and Rock, you fool, you said I wouldn't be able to get gray there.....||||reg||1
Z||000011||donalson||09-11-2001||03:04 AM||||um this is kinda ghetto...but looks pretty good<P>the family suburban...it had the "tent" going...my dad ripped it out...scraped off all the foam crap...and sprayed it a color that matched the body color...it looks good...much better then a "tent" and it was cheap...just soem time and like $3 for paint<P>mark||||reg||1
Z||000012||MontanaFiero||09-11-2001||04:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>You can pick up a headliner kit called "Heads Up". It's available in many colors.<BR>For sale at Trak Auto, AutoZone, PepBoys, ETC. The Heads Up stuff is thicker than what you'd get at a fabric shop. I don't know about stuff from an upholstery shop.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>But-- have you tried using this stuff on a vehicle with a sunroof?  When I did my conversion I cut a hole in my original "coupe" style headliner which I quickly found to be molded differently---a disaster. My car looks like it has rags hanging down from the ceiling.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
